  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1034 AM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nStarting the long term period for Sunday and Monday, dry conditions \nwill continue. Some diurnally breezy conditions are also expected\nwith a developing sinusoidal pattern over the western CONUS. Net \nresult is some mixing and warm temperatures, but should remain \ndry. Highs for this time period will remain above average for \nearly October. Going into Tuesday, a notable perturbation within \nthe main synoptic mid level SW flow may move towards the \nPanhandles. In the most aggressive model datasets, a narrow \ncorridor of 99th percentile (+3 S.D. for October climatology) \nadvects into the Panhandles downstream of a deepening H500 trough \nover southern California and upstream of broad H500 high over the \nNW Gulf coast. This could set up the potential for training and/or\nrepeat rounds of thunderstorms. Watching the potential for some \nsevere storms. Still several days out with many factors to watch \nfor this potential on Tuesday, so check back fir the latest \nupdates to the forecast. Continued rain chances also to watch \nthrough the end of the forecast period with temperatures near \naverage toward the middle of next week.",
